1
00:00:05,047 --> 00:00:09,775
Every decision makes waves. Ripple lets you see them before you decide.

2
00:00:09,775 --> 00:00:13,958
Decisions often get made without hearing from the people they affect.

3
00:00:13,958 --> 00:00:25,530
Ripple simulates 1,000 people. As you scroll, a year passes and opinions spread.

4
00:00:25,530 --> 00:00:29,527
Type any decision. Ripple reads it as you type.

5
00:00:29,527 --> 00:00:33,730
It simulates 1,000 students, teachers and families…

6
00:00:33,730 --> 00:00:39,361
…and starts from real polls. Banning every device gets very little support.

7
00:00:39,361 --> 00:00:56,552
Ripple suggests a narrower version and tests it by re-running the simulation.

8
00:00:56,552 --> 00:01:00,355
Phones only during class: 68% of adults support that in a Pew Research poll.

9
00:01:00,355 --> 00:01:06,237
Share a link that reproduces the exact result, or an image card.

10
00:01:06,237 --> 00:01:10,688
Optional: Claude can write a full report from the simulation’s data.

11
00:01:10,688 --> 00:01:22,937
Watch the crowd make up its mind over a year.

12
00:01:22,937 --> 00:01:28,131
Hear what each group would say, in its own words.

13
00:01:28,131 --> 00:01:35,496
…and a town hall where the voices answer each other.

14
00:01:35,496 --> 00:01:41,704
Enter a ZIP code and Ripple builds the crowd from your district’s real Census data.

15
00:01:41,704 --> 00:01:47,460
It shows who represents you, and how your district compares with the country.

16
00:01:47,460 --> 00:01:52,704
25 real bills from Congress, checked against Congress.gov.

17
00:01:52,704 --> 00:02:00,347
Read what a bill does, see how far it got, and simulate it — even in your own district.

18
00:02:00,347 --> 00:02:09,986
Then take it further: who decides, and a letter to your representative that cites real polls.

19
00:02:09,986 --> 00:02:17,747
Ripple is a rehearsal. Send a 30-second survey to real people.

20
00:02:17,747 --> 00:02:26,224
As answers come in, they appear live next to Ripple’s prediction, group by group.

21
00:02:26,224 --> 00:02:36,330
Compare two wordings with the same crowd. Words change who’s with you.

22
00:02:36,330 --> 00:02:43,491
Every number shows its source, and Ripple checks itself against real polls.
